<!DOCTYPE html>
<html>
<head>
<title>AED Program Manual</title>
<style>
  @page { size: A4; margin: 0; }
  .page {
    width: 794px; height: 1123px;
    padding: 50px 60px; box-sizing: border-box;
    overflow: hidden; page-break-after: always;
    position: relative;
    font-family: "DejaVu Serif", "Liberation Serif", Georgia, "Helvetica", Arial, "DejaVu Sans", "Liberation Sans";
  }
  .page:last-child { page-break-after: auto; }
  h1, h2, h3, h4 { font-weight: bold; }
  .header-info { display: flex; justify-content: space-between; align-items: center; margin-bottom: 20px; }
  .section-header { display: flex; justify-content: space-between; margin-bottom: 15px; }
  .content-section { margin-bottom: 20px; }
  .list-item { margin-bottom: 10px; }
  table { width: 100%; border-collapse: collapse; margin-top: 15px; }
  td { padding: 8px 0; }
  .signature-block { margin-top: 50px; }
</style>
</head>
<body>
<div class="page">
  <div class="header-info">
    <div>
      <span data-field="document_title">{{ document_title }}</span>
    </div>
    <div>
      <span data-field="document_id">{{ document_id }}</span>
    </div>
  </div>

  <div class="section-header">
    <div>
      <span data-field="section_title">{{ section_title }}</span>
    </div>
    <div>
      <span data-field="document_title_2">{{ document_title_2 }}</span>
    </div>
  </div>

  <div class="section-header">
    <div>
      <strong>SECTION AREA:</strong> <span data-field="section_area">{{ section_area }}</span>
    </div>
    <div>
      <strong>MAPP:</strong> <span data-field="mapp_number">{{ mapp_number }}</span>
    </div>
  </div>

  <div class="content-section">
    <div class="section-header">
      <strong>SUBJECT:</strong> <span data-field="subject">{{ subject }}</span>
    </div>
  </div>

  <div class="content-section">
    <h3>I. POLICY</h3>
    <div class="list-item">
      <p>A. It is <span data-field="university_name">{{ university_name }}</span> policy to comply with safety-related regulations that govern the University's operations, and to protect the safety of the University's faculty, staff, and students. The LU Environmental Health and Safety (EHS) Office develops safety-related policies and programs to accomplish this objective.</p>
    </div>
  </div>

  <div class="content-section">
    <h3>II. PURPOSE AND SCOPE</h3>
    <div class="list-item">
      <p>A. This document informs LU faculty, staff, and students of the Automated External Defibrillator (AED) program policies and procedures. This document applies to all persons who visit or work on the University campus.</p>
    </div>
    <div class="list-item">
      <p>B. This document was created to provide an AED responder general guidance for the rapid response to a sudden cardiac arrest (SCA).</p>
    </div>
  </div>

  <div class="content-section">
    <h3>III. DEFINITIONS</h3>
    <div class="list-item">
      <p>A. <strong>Automated External Defibrillator (AED).</strong> A device that automatically analyzes heart rhythms and advises the operator to deliver a shock if necessary. Lay responders can use AEDs safely and effectively with minimal training.</p>
    </div>
    <div class="list-item">
      <p>B. <strong>AED Responder.</strong> An employee who is appropriately trained and certified to operate an AED Unit during his/her time at work.</p>
    </div>
    <div class="list-item">
      <p>C. <strong>AED Program.</strong> Program led by EHS that includes oversight of the installation and post-installation maintenance of the AEDs, training of employees, and safety and compliance.</p>
    </div>
    <div class="list-item">
      <p>D. <strong>Building Coordinator.</strong> Each building on campus has an employee who has been named as Building Coordinator and is responsible for a building. This employee will assist EHS with the AED Program.</p>
    </div>
  </div>
</div>

<div class="page">
  <div class="header-info">
    <div>
      <span data-field="document_title">{{ document_title }}</span>
    </div>
    <div>
      <span data-field="document_id">{{ document_id }}</span>
    </div>
  </div>

  <div class="content-section">
    <h3>IV. RESPONSIBILITIES</h3>
    <div class="list-item">
      <p>A. <strong>EHS.</strong> It is the responsibility of EHS to:</p>
      <ol>
        <li class="list-item">Provide oversight of the installation and post-installation maintenance of the AEDs, training of employees, and safety and compliance.</li>
        <li class="list-item">Ensure regular maintenance of the AED Units and related response equipment.</li>
        <li class="list-item">Assist Building Coordinators with AED Program. May provide training in maintenance procedures and assistance with scheduling AED training for employees, including for Building Coordinator.</li>
        <li class="list-item">Develop and maintain the AED emergency response plan and system policies and procedures and review the program annually to evaluate effectiveness.</li>
        <li class="list-item">Assure compliance with state and local regulations regarding AED use.</li>
        <li class="list-item">Maintain a list of AED Responders and their training records and share the list, including additions and changes, with the appropriate Building Coordinator(s).</li>
        <li class="list-item">Maintain records pertinent to the AED program and assures responsibilities delegated to others as outlined in this policy are met.</li>
      </ol>
    </div>
    <div class="list-item">
      <p>B. <strong>Building Coordinator.</strong> It is the responsibility of Building Coordinators to:</p>
      <ol>
        <li class="list-item">Report any noticeable device defects, or missing, expired, and/or damaged accessories to EHS immediately.</li>
        <li class="list-item">Receive from EHS the list of trained AED Responders in their building and familiarize themselves with individuals in their building who can serve as AED Responders.</li>
        <li class="list-item">Ensure compliance with the policies and procedures of the AED Program.</li>
        <li class="list-item">Assure compliance with state and local regulations regarding AED use.</li>
      </ol>
    </div>
    <div class="list-item">
      <p><em>Note. LU's Office of Facilities Management has oversight of the Building Coordinator Policy (MAPP).</em></p>
    </div>
    <div class="list-item">
      <p>C. <strong>AED Responders.</strong> It is the responsibility of AED Responders to:</p>
      <ol>
        <li class="list-item">Successfully complete all required AED training and skills evaluations.</li>
        <li class="list-item">Follow the guidelines of the AED program and remain current on the AED training required by <span data-field="university_name">{{ university_name }}</span>.</li>
        <li class="list-item">Communicate with EHS regarding their AED Responder status (training, assignment to another building, departure from LU, etc.).</li>
        <li class="list-item">Respond to all SCA incidents in assigned building.</li>
        <li class="list-item">Immediately after an SCA incident in assigned building, communicate with EHS to document the incident.</li>
      </ol>
    </div>
  </div>

  <div class="content-section">
    <h3>V. REVIEW AND RESPONSIBILITY</h3>
    <div class="list-item">
      <p><strong>Responsible Party:</strong> <span data-field="responsible_party">{{ responsible_party }}</span></p>
    </div>
    <div class="list-item">
      <p><strong>Review:</strong> Every two years on or before August 1</p>
    </div>
  </div>
</div>

<div class="page">
  <div class="header-info">
    <div>
      <span data-field="document_title">{{ document_title }}</span>
    </div>
    <div>
      <span data-field="document_id">{{ document_id }}</span>
    </div>
  </div>

  <div class="content-section">
    <h3>VI. APPROVAL</h3>
    <table style="width: 100%;">
      <tr>
        <td style="width: 50%;">
          <p>_________________________</p>
          <p>Edward Craig Ness</p>
          <p>Vice President for Finance and Operations</p>
          <p>Date</p>
        </td>
        <td style="width: 50%;">
          <p>_________________________</p>
          <p>Kenneth R. Evans</p>
          <p>President</p>
          <p>Date</p>
        </td>
      </tr>
    </table>
  </div>

  <div class="content-section">
    <h3>REVISION LOG</h3>
    <table>
      <thead>
        <tr>
          <td style="width: 10%;">Revision Number</td>
          <td style="width: 20%;">Date</td>
          <td style="width: 70%;">Description of Changes</td>
        </tr>
      </thead>
      <tbody>
        <tr>
          <td>1</td>
          <td>08/01/2017</td>
          <td>Initial version.</td>
        </tr>
        <tr>
          <td>2</td>
          <td>08/22/2019</td>
          <td>Revised version approved by President.</td>
        </tr>
        <tr>
          <td>3</td>
          <td>09/17/2019, 11/05/2019</td>
          <td>Clarified & updated the roles & responsibilities of EHS, Building Coordinators, and AED Responders. Made changes in format and wording to bring MAPP in line with standardized MAPP format and language.</td>
        </tr>
        <tr>
          <td>4</td>
          <td>01/09/2020</td>
          <td>Updated MAPP approved by President.</td>
        </tr>
      </tbody>
    </table>
  </div>

  <div style="margin-top: 80px; text-align: right;">
    <p>Approved: <span data-field="approval_date">{{ approval_date }}</span>; revised <span data-field="revision_date">{{ revision_date }}</span></p>
    <p>Page 3 of 3</p>
  </div>
</div>
</body>
</html>